This extension adds Batman: Arkham City modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]TFC Installer will be installed automatically.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00]This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/588?tab=description]TFC Installer for UE2/3[/url]. This allows you to install texture mods and other types of mods that update the game data archives.[/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]TFC Installer installs to the game folder, recognised by a "tfcinstaller.exe" file.[/*]
[*]UPK Explorer installs to the game folder, recognised by a "upk explorer.exe" file.[/*]
[*]TFC mods with a "gameprofile.xml" file or a ".packagepatch" file install to the "TFCInstaller\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "BmGame" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Cooked Sub Folder mods with a "SFX" folder or a ".upk" file install to the "BmGame\CookedPCConsole" folder.[/*]
[*]Movies mods with a ".bik" file install to the "BmGame\Movies" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods with a "BmLauncher.exe" file or a ".exe" file install to the "Binaries\Win32" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff00]Downloads and installs TFC Installer automatically.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Installs TFC Installer mods to "TFCInstaller&#92;Mods" folder. You need to run the automatically downloaded tool from the Dashboard in Vortex to install those mods to the game archives.[/*]
[*]Includes a tool for UPK Explorer. The tool will be installed to the "UPK Explorer" folder.[/*]
[*][color=#a4c2f4][b]For TFC mods, you must install them using the included tool after installing with Vortex.[/b][/color][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Batman: Arkham City mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

TFC Installer (tool):

This installer handles the TFC Installer, not mods for it. It exists so users can install the TFC Installer through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "tfcinstaller.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle the TFC Installer inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as the TFC Installer rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list the TFC Installer as a requirement.

========================================================================

UPK Explorer (tool):

This installer handles UPK Explorer, not mods for it. It exists so users can install UPK Explorer through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "upk explorer.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle UPK Explorer inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as UPK Explorer rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list UPK Explorer as a requirement.

========================================================================

TFC Mods:

Texture/content mods handled through the TFC system.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "gameprofile.xml", "gameprofile.idremappings.xml", "objectdescriptors.xml", "packageextensions.xml", "texturepack" or "game".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".packagepatch", ".descriptor", ".tfcmapping" or ".inipatch" extensions.

  Installs to: "TFCInstaller\Mods"

  Common mistakes:
    - Keep the original file names - the TFC system matches them by name.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── BmGame\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "BmGame", "engine", "Binaries", "Config", "CookedPCConsole", "Localization" or "Movies" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Cooked Content Mods:

Packaged content deployed into the game's cooked content folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "SFX" in the archive.
    - Recognised by any file with the ".upk" extension.

  Installs to: "BmGame\CookedPCConsole"

========================================================================

Movie / Cutscene Replacements:

Replacement video files, deployed into the game's movies folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".bik" extension.

  Installs to: "BmGame\Movies"

  Common mistakes:
    - The replacement must keep the original file name, or the game will not pick it up.

========================================================================

Binaries / Injector Mods:

DLL injectors and other files that belong next to the game executable.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "BmLauncher.exe".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".exe", ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" extensions.

  Installs to: "Binaries\Win32"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

